# AI
.omc
docs/superpowers
.envrc
.claude
# Anchored. Without the leading slash git matches these against every path
# segment, and on a case-insensitive filesystem `SECURITY.md` also matches
# `site/content/docs/security.md` — which silently kept the Security page's
# source out of the repository while its built HTML stayed committed.
/DO_MARKETPLACE.md
/INTEGRATIONS.md
/SECURITY.md
.stohr
.screenshots
screenshots

sdks/swift/.build
# dependencies (bun install)
node_modules

# output
out
dist
*.tgz

# code coverage
coverage
*.lcov

# logs
# Anchored: an unanchored `logs` matches every path segment, which silently
# excluded src/logs/ and src/api/routes/logs/ and shipped a server that could
# not start. The same shape once swallowed site/content/docs/security.md.
/logs
*.log
report.[0-9]_.[0-9]_.[0-9]_.[0-9]_.json

# dotenv environment variable files — match every form except the example.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

